Can anyone let me know the most efficient way to code

result = m[sample(which(a < x < b), 1),]

in TMB. In the above R code, m is a matrix, x is a numeric vector, and a and b are numeric.

One potential way is to use std::shuffle/random_shuffle, although, I am not sure if these
routines are compatible with TMB objects or whether this is even an optimal approach?

some pseudo code describing what i'm considering is,

#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>

std::vector<int> v ... // vector of indices to loop over 0:n_i
std::random_shuffle(v.begin(), v.end()); //randomize indices

for(i=0; i<n_i; i++) {
  if(a < x(v(i)) < b) {
    result = m.row(v(i)) // save result
    break // end loop
  }
}

Any help is appreciated,

Chris

